To solve the system of equations \begin{align*}
5x-2y&=7,\\
3x+y&=2,
\end{align*}we first eliminate $y$. Multiplying the second equation by 2 gives us \begin{align*}
6x+2y&=4.\end{align*}Adding this to the first equation eliminates $y$ and gives us \begin{align*}
11x&=11,\end{align*}so $x=1$. Substituting $x=1$ into the second equation gives us $3(1)+y=2$, so $y=-1$. To compute $24x-14y$, we substitute $x=1$ and $y=-1$ to get \begin{align*}24(1)-14(-1)&=24+14\\)&=\boxed{38}.\endthought> <answer>38</answer>

